.TH DAGNABIT 1 "2026-04-17" "dagnabit 0.1.0" "Developer Tools"
.SH NAME
dagnabit \- reposition Go packages by dependency depth and generate export facades
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dagnabit
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-depth
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-initial ]
.RB [ \-module
.IR path ]
.IR prefix ...
.PP
.B dagnabit export
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-output\-dir
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-module
.IR path ]
.RI [ packages... ]
.PP
.B dagnabit move
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.RB [ \-module
.IR path ]
.IR src
.IR dst
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dagnabit
is a Go code organization tool with three subcommands: repositioning,
export facade generation, and package relocation.
.PP
Without a subcommand,
.B dagnabit
analyzes the dependency graph of Go packages using
.BR "go list" ,
computes a topological sort, and moves packages into directories
named after NATO phonetic levels based on their dependency depth.
Leaf packages (no internal dependencies) go to level 0, their
dependents to alfa, and so on up through the NATO alphabet.
.PP
The
.B export
subcommand generates facade packages that re-export symbols from
.I internal/
packages, creating a public API surface in
.IR pkgs/ .
Types are re-exported as aliases, non-generic functions and variables
as var bindings, and constants as const bindings.
Generic functions are wrapped because Go does not support assigning
them to variables without instantiation (see
.UR https://github.com/golang/go/issues/52654
golang/go#52654\c
.UE ).
Functions whose signatures reference unexported types are skipped.
.PP
Code generation uses
.B jennifer
(github.com/dave/jennifer) for proper import management.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS "reposition (default)"
Analyze and reposition packages based on dependency depth.
Must be run from a directory containing
.IR go.mod .
.SS "move"
Relocate a single Go package from
.I src
to
.I dst
(both relative to the module root). When the leaf directory name differs
between
.I src
and
.IR dst ,
.B move
performs type-aware rewrites of the package's
.B package
declaration and of qualified references (e.g.,
.IB oldLeaf .X
\(->
.IB newLeaf .X )
in every caller, using
.B golang.org/x/tools/go/packages
to discriminate package uses from local variables, aliased imports, and
dot-imports.
.PP
A pre-move analysis aborts if
.B packages.Load
reports any type errors in the module. Pass
.B \-\-force
to proceed anyway.
.SS "export"
Generate
.I pkgs/
facade files from
.I internal/
packages.
.PP
After generation, if a
.BR treefmt (1)
configuration
.RB ( treefmt.toml ,
.BR .treefmt.toml ,
or
.BR treefmt.nix )
is found by walking up from the module root,
.B dagnabit
runs the formatter on the output directory. Resolution prefers the
.B treefmt
binary on
.BR PATH ;
if absent and the config is
.BR treefmt.nix ,
falls back to
.B nix fmt
with the output dir as a positional argument. This is skipped under
.B \-\-dry\-run
and when neither tool is available.
.PP
Three invocation modes:
.TP
.B "dagnabit export"
Scan
.I internal/
for files containing
.B //go:generate dagnabit export
directives and generate facades for each.
.TP
.BI "dagnabit export " packages...
Generate facades for the specified package patterns
(e.g.,
.BR ./internal/alfa/... ).
.TP
.B "//go:generate dagnabit export"
Place this directive in a source file within an internal package.
Run
.B go generate
to invoke dagnabit for that package.
.SH POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IR prefix ...
One or more package tree prefixes to analyze (e.g.
.BR lib ", " internal ", " src ).
At least one prefix is required for the reposition subcommand.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Reposition options"
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be moved without moving.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output.
.TP
.BI \-depth " N"
Path component depth: 3 for
.I prefix/level/package
(default), 2 for
.IR level/package .
Use depth 2 for repos where NATO levels are top-level directories.
Implied (and overridden) by
.BR \-\-initial .
.TP
.B \-\-initial
Initial tiering of a flat
.I <prefix>/<pkg>
layout. Inserts a NATO level segment into every package path based on
its dependency height, producing
.IR <prefix>/<level>/<pkg> .
Implies
.BR "\-depth 2" .
.TP
.BI \-module " path"
Go module path. Read from
.I go.mod
if empty.
.SS "Move options"
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be moved without moving. Prints counts of package-decl
rewrites and qualified-reference rewrite sites.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Proceed even if
.B packages.Load
reports type errors. Rewrites may miss call sites in packages with type
errors; use only when the errors are unrelated to the moved package.
.TP
.BI \-module " path"
Go module path. Read from
.I go.mod
if empty.
.SS "Export options"
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be generated without writing files.
.TP
.BI \-output\-dir " dir"
Output directory for generated facades, relative to the module root
(default:
.BR pkgs ).
.TP
.BI \-module " path"
Go module path. Read from
.I go.mod
if empty.
.SH EXAMPLES
Reposition packages in a repo with
.I lib/
and
.I internal/
prefixes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cd myproject
dagnabit -n -v lib internal
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reposition packages in a repo where NATO levels are top-level:
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit -n -v -depth 2 0 alfa bravo charlie
.fi
.RE
.PP
Initial tiering of a flat
.I internal/<pkg>
layout (produces
.IR internal/0/<pkg> ", " internal/alfa/<pkg> ", \fR\(aq.\(aq\fP\ etc.):
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit -n -v --initial internal
.fi
.RE
.PP
Relocate a package with a leaf rename (rewrites package decl, imports,
and qualified references in callers):
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit move internal/foo internal/bar
.fi
.RE
.PP
Relocate without renaming the leaf (same leaf, imports-only rewrite):
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit move internal/alfa/foo internal/bravo/foo
.fi
.RE
.PP
Dry-run a move to preview what would change:
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit move -n internal/foo internal/bar
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate export facades for all marked internal packages:
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit export
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate facades for specific packages:
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit export ./internal/alfa/blob_store_id ./internal/bravo/...
.fi
.RE
.PP
Dry-run to see what would be generated:
.PP
.RS
.nf
dagnabit export -n ./internal/...
.fi
.RE
.SH GENERATED OUTPUT
For an internal package at
.IR internal/alfa/blob_store_id ,
dagnabit generates
.IR pkgs/blob_store_id/main.go :
.PP
.RS
.nf
// Code generated by dagnabit; DO NOT EDIT.

package blob_store_id

import internal "example.com/mod/internal/alfa/blob_store_id"

type (
    Id           = internal.Id
    LocationType = internal.LocationType
)

var (
    Make             = internal.Make
    MakeWithLocation = internal.MakeWithLocation
)
.fi
.RE
.SH DIRECTIVES
Place the following comment in any
.I .go
file within an internal package to mark it for export:
.PP
.RS
.B //go:generate dagnabit export
.RE
.PP
When
.B dagnabit export
is run without arguments, it scans
.I internal/
for this directive.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (dependency cycle, missing go.mod, generation failure, etc.).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR go-generate (1),
.BR go-list (1),
.BR treefmt (1)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/amarbel-llc/purse-first/issues
.UE .
